    "faq_xtrnXw": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "accordion_HQxThJ": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What's the difference between adhesive and sew-on hook and loop tape?",
            "content": "<p>The adhesive hook and loop is dead simple for some fast jobs. Just peel the back off and slap it on smooth stuff—walls, cables, whatever hard surface you've got. No sewing mess. But sew-on? That's for fabric like your clothes or sofa bits; you stitch it right in, and it hangs tough way past when glue gives up.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_bwj8Ec": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is hook and loop strong enough for heavy-duty jobs?",
            "content": "<p>Yeah, regular hook and loop handles everyday stuff like cables or light holds, no dramas. For heavy gear like van panels, tools, grab the heavy-duty. Thicker build, grips bite hard, won't let go, whatever the load.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_aknekp": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I cut hook and loop fastening tape to size at home?",
            "content": "<p>No worries, household scissors do the trick, it's soft enough to slice any length straight from the roll, dead easy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_9hAAYD": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do I get the adhesive to actually stick and stay put?",
            "content": "<p>To start, scrubbing and cleaning the oil or dust is enough to mess it up. Then push down really firm, all even-like, and walk away for 24 hours at least. Don't pile weight on early! Do that, and you've got a bond that'll last ages.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_E3rbmx": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do you ship hook and loop tape across all of Australia?",
            "content": "<p>We sure do, right to your door anywhere in Oz, quick and no fuss, 'cause we've got over 100,000 metres stacked up ready. Hit $300 on the order, and shipping's free. Easy as, wherever you're at.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
